   "text": {
    "L1": "Special places can be fragile. Visitors can harm them without meaning to.",
    "L2": "Litter, loud noise, feeding animals, and leaving paths all cause harm.",
    "L3": "One small careless act may seem unimportant. Repeated by thousands, it becomes big damage.",
    "L4": "Myth: visiting a place cannot harm it. That is not true because every visitor's actions add up.",
    "L5": "Responsible visitors carry waste back, use refillable bottles, and stay on paths.",
    "L6": "They keep quiet near animals, never feed wildlife, and follow local rules and guides.",
    "L7": "Respect the place and the people who live there. Leave the special place safe for others."
   },
